  "key_evidence_summary": "Only checkoutservice shows restart churn in namespace boutique: pod checkoutservice-7f88d56cf6-zjb4s reports RESTARTS 2 (30s ago) then 3, all other 10 boutique pods at 0. Pod detail: Last State Terminated, Reason Error, Exit Code 2; Ready False. Pod events: 'Warning Unhealthy (x9): Liveness probe failed: Get \"http://172.20.2.169:5050/\": net/http: HTTP/1.x transport connection broken: malformed HTTP response \"\\x00\\x00\\x06\\x04...\"' followed by 'Normal Killing (x3): Container server failed liveness probe, will be restarted'. The returned byte string is HTTP/2/gRPC framing, because checkoutservice is a gRPC server: GetAppYAML(checkoutservice) shows livenessProbe httpGet {path: /, port: 5050} while readinessProbe correctly uses grpc {port: 5050}, the Service port is named 'grpc', and container logs show 'starting to listen on tcp: \"[::]:5050\"'. So the liveness probe probes a gRPC port with HTTP/1.x, fails forever, and kubelet kills the container in a loop. No OOMKilled (no 137, no memory event) and no scheduling/volume/DNS anomaly; no active alerts.",
